 A related result is <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Proposition 6.5</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Dwyer-Greenlees">Dwyer-Greenlees</a>]</span>. The derived Nakayama lemma can for example be found in Bhatt's 3rd lecture on Prismatic cohomology at Columbia University in Fall 2018 as Section 2 property (2). Leonid Positselski proposed a proof in <a href="https://mathoverflow.net/a/331501">https://mathoverflow.net/a/331501</a>. However, we follow the proof suggested by Anonymous in the comments. 